7. Exploration Rules

The player can freely explore the civilization.

However, certain locations have restrictions.

Pyramid Areas

The player can approach and explore around many pyramid locations.

Some internal areas are restricted.

Construction Zones

Active construction zones are especially restricted.

The player cannot simply walk into every construction area.

He can observe certain activities from permitted locations.

This makes the player feel like he is actually exploring a functioning ancient civilization rather than a museum.

---

8. Seven Pyramids

There are seven major pyramids connected to the civilization's history.

Their individual purposes and stories are different.

Pyramid 1 — Mummy Queen

The Mummy Queen pyramid contains the story of an ancient queen who was believed to have received a divine blessing that prevented her from truly dying.

People became afraid of her.

When the player encounters her, she does NOT attack him.

Instead, she wants someone to listen to her story.

Most people run away from her.

The player can choose not to run.

If the player stays, the Mummy Queen explains her backstory.

This becomes one of the chapter's major mysterious encounters.

---

Pyramid 2 — The Great King

The second major pyramid is connected to the Great King.

The Great King is no longer alive.

Only his burial/cover remains.

People around the civilization spread rumors that people who enter the pyramid may never return.

Nobody completely knows the truth.

The actual history behind this pyramid becomes part of the mystery.

---

Pyramid 3 — Divine Pyramid

The third pyramid is connected to the ancient civilization's religious beliefs.

It was built for the worship of their gods/deities rather than simply for the burial of a ruler.

The deeper meaning of this pyramid is connected to the civilization's ancient beliefs.

Some of its history is intentionally mysterious.

---

Pyramid 4 — The Greatest Gift

The fourth pyramid was built by a king for his queen.

The king wanted to give the queen:

«"The greatest gift in the world."»

He therefore ordered the construction of an enormous pyramid.

This pyramid is intentionally much larger than the others.

Its purpose is not death or burial.

It is simply an enormous royal gift.

The king's idea is partly romantic and partly ridiculous.

The construction therefore creates many comedy opportunities.

Unfinished Top

After approximately 1,000 years, the pyramid's upper section is still unfinished.

Several huge stones remain.

The original workers died long ago, and later civilizations never completed the work because they did not consider it important.

JCB Achievement

In the modern/gameplay era, the player may purchase/use a JCB-like machine to complete the remaining construction.

If the player completes the structure, a special achievement is unlocked.

The achievement is intentionally misleading.

The ancient King and Queen's spirits appear and bless the machine, not the player.

Because the player is standing in front of the machine, the player assumes the blessing belongs to him.

However, JCB technology did not exist during the ancient period.

This creates a hidden comedy Easter egg.

---

Pyramid 5 — Ancient Pyramid Competition

The fifth pyramid was not created for a king, queen, god, or burial.

It originated from an ancient pyramid-building competition.

Different teams competed to create the best pyramid design.

The winning design became the fifth pyramid.

The player can potentially discover this competition through the past timeline.

The player may also participate in the competition with his team.

If the player's team wins, the result can create a timeline-related consequence.

The player's actions can influence certain historical outcomes.

This is one of the systems where the player can interfere with the timeline.

---

Pyramid 6 — Twin Stone Pyramid

The sixth pyramid was created in connection with the 100-year legacy of a King and Queen.

The structure contains two different types of stone.

The two stones represent the King and Queen remaining together.

Important royal possessions were placed inside.

By the modern era, the possessions have become extremely old, damaged, and rusted.

Some replicas of ancient objects may later appear in shops.

The pyramid therefore connects the ancient royal story with modern exploration.

---

Pyramid 7 — Pyramid of Echoes

The seventh pyramid is completely different from the others.

It was created by ancient scientists.

Their original experiments were focused on:

- Improving arrow speed
- Improving arrow distance
- Sending sound farther
- Understanding echoes
- Long-distance communication
- Communication between different locations

They were experimenting with ways to make communication possible across large distances.

The pyramid contains chambers designed around sound and echoes.

A sound created in one chamber can travel through the structure and produce an unexpected response somewhere else.

Hidden Communication Mystery

The ancient scientists gradually realize that distance does not necessarily need to prevent communication.

The deeper purpose of their work becomes connected to the idea of connecting people across great distances.

---

9. The Hidden Inscription

Deep inside the Pyramid of Echoes is a hidden inscription.

It is not openly visible.

Most people do not know it exists.

The inscription uses Morse Code and extremely difficult archaic English.

Morse Layer

The first layer contains a coded message.

The player must decode the Morse Code.

The decoded message leads to a difficult English statement.

Difficult English Layer

The inscription contains an extremely archaic sentence:

«"Though the uttermost expanse of the terrestrial realm should sunder two souls beyond the compass of mortal traversal, let neither intervening distance nor profoundest silence render their reciprocal utterance bereft of communion."»

Meaning

The message means:

«"Even if enormous distance separates two people, distance and silence should not prevent them from communicating with each other."»

The player must research the difficult English to understand the message.

This inscription becomes a subtle historical clue toward future communication technology.

---

10. Player's Main Objective

The chapter begins with a mysterious objective:

«"Determine the nature of this unfamiliar realm and uncover the reason for thy presence within it."»

Meaning:

«Find out where you are and why you are here.»

As the player discovers more about the civilization, the objective evolves:

«"Unravel the civilization surrounding thee and seek the means by which thy return may be attained."»

Meaning:

«Understand this ancient civilization and find a way to return.»

Objectives throughout the chapter use deliberately difficult, archaic English.

The player should feel that the game itself is communicating through an ancient civilization.

