11. King Election System

At a later point in the civilization's story, the current King dies.

The civilization needs a new King.

The player and other eligible characters can become candidates.

The people vote to determine who should become the next King.

The player does NOT automatically become King.

The player's previous actions affect his reputation.

Factors may include:

- Helping NPCs
- Completing important tasks
- Making good decisions
- Building relationships
- Helping the civilization
- Gaining support from important NPCs

The player may win the election.

If the player becomes King, he gains the ability to influence parts of the civilization.

He may make certain decisions about:

- Construction
- Pyramid projects
- Civilization development
- Royal decisions
- Future historical events

This can affect the timeline.

The player may eventually realize:

«"I am not just visiting this history. I can change it."»

---

12. Team System

The desert experience has a special team system.

When entering this world, the player can choose whether to invite other players.

Players can form a team with:

- Friends
- Other players
- NPCs

The maximum server/team size is flexible depending on server performance.

The system may dynamically allow approximately:

- 5 players under high server load
- 10 players under moderate load
- Up to 20 players when server performance allows

The exact limit is determined by server performance.

There is no fixed role system.

Players decide among themselves who handles which task.

One player may investigate.

Another may explore.

Another may interact with NPCs.

Another may handle transportation.

Players can also joke around and explore together.

The entire team experiences the same story progression.

---

13. Vehicles and Transportation

The desert supports multiple forms of transportation.

Camel

The camel is the most useful natural form of desert transportation.

Camels are not automatically free.

Players may need to purchase or obtain them from local people.

Vehicles

Other vehicles may also be available.

Every transportation method has advantages and disadvantages.

For example:

- Some vehicles may be faster.
- Some may struggle in sand.
- Some may get stuck.
- Camels may perform better in certain desert areas.

The player chooses based on the situation.

---

14. Shops

Ancient shops can appear throughout the civilization.

They sell replicas or ancient-style objects such as:

- Small pyramid models
- Ancient clothing
- Decorative objects
- Mummy-themed items
- Ancient tools
- Collectible objects

Children and NPCs may wear or show off some of these objects.

These objects can later become useful clues or references during exploration.

